WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.760
Spider-Man and Venom: two great&nbsp;
tastes that taste great together.
 &nbsp;

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.400
"Yummy."
 
The multiverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.720
cracked wide open in "Spider-Man: No Way Home,"&nbsp;
paving the way for all sorts of characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.800
bad and good, to make the leap across franchises&nbsp;
and enter the Marvel Cinematic Universe.&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.000
In a crossover foreshadowed by the&nbsp;
post-credits scene of Sony's "Venom:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.920
Let There Be Carnage," the Lethal Protector&nbsp;
himself shows up in the first post-credits scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.680
of "No Way Home," which it picks up shortly&nbsp;
after the "Venom" sequel's shocking tease.&nbsp;

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.920
After seeming to cross universes in "Let There Be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.880
Carnage," and seeing a news report&nbsp;
about Tom Holland's Spider-Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.200
"No Way Home" definitively confirms that Venom&nbsp;
and Eddie Brock were pulled into the MCU.&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.360
The "No Way Home" footage shows Eddie and Venom&nbsp;
seated at a bar, as the symbiote's human host&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.760
comes to terms with everything MCU-related.&nbsp;
That includes Thanos, the Infinity Stones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.600
Iron Man, and the Blip, thanks to a patient&nbsp;
bartender who's there to explain it all.&nbsp;

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.040
But when Eddie suggests that he and Venom&nbsp;
go and see Spider-Man in New York to talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.400
about their situation, he and Venom are&nbsp;
suddenly pulled back to their universe.&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.000
These events leave fans with a pretty&nbsp;
big question after the dramatic events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.320
of "Spider-Man: No Way Home": Will Venom&nbsp;
ever come face-to-face with Spider-Man?&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.800
Some form of Venom and Spider-Man fighting one&nbsp;
another on screen again seems like a sure thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.120
not only because they've fought&nbsp;
in the world of Marvel Comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.360
but also because Sony Pictures holds the rights&nbsp;
to both the Spider and the Symbiote. The only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:20.560
potential roadblock here is Marvel Studios head&nbsp;
Kevin Feige and the studio's plans for the MCU.
 &nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.040
"The entire relationship between Sony and&nbsp;
Marvel and Disney is really unprecedented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:28.320
in Hollywood history, and it's all&nbsp;
because everyone loves Spider-Man."
 &nbsp;

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.720
Thankfully, Sony and Marvel seem to have formed a&nbsp;
solid working relationship, so it's highly likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.480
Tom Holland and Tom Hardy will share the&nbsp;
screen in a Marvel adventure at some point.&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.480
That said, it's not hard to throw two Marvel&nbsp;
characters together and shout "Fight!"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:45.040
A compelling plot will go a long way to making the&nbsp;
meeting of these two figures feel natural. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.360
all, a lot of legwork had to be done to get them&nbsp;
in the same universe, let alone the same arena.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.280
The most important thing seems to be carving&nbsp;
out a story for their matchup that makes sense.
 &nbsp;

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.720
"Please, Scooby-Doo this crap."
 
When asked about the prospect of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:00.960
a crossover in the wake of "Venom: Let There&nbsp;
Be Carnage," Holland told Total Film Magazine,&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.800
"I genuinely don't know. It was really&nbsp;
exciting to be a part of that film. Obviously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:09.040
Tom Hardy is one of the greatest actors in the&nbsp;
world. I'm happy to say that he's a lovely bloke.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:13.360
But I haven't really given it very much thought."
Meanwhile, back in August, Hardy told Esquire,&nbsp;

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:16.960
"I would be remiss if I wasn't trying to&nbsp;
steer any kind of connectivity. Obviously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:21.200
that's a large canyon to leap, to be bridged by&nbsp;
one person alone, and it would take a much higher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:26.240
level of diplomacy and intelligence, sitting down&nbsp;
and talking, to take on an arena such as that."&nbsp;

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.840
The only question left to ask is how the&nbsp;
two characters might meet up in the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.520
and the answer possibly lies in the "No&nbsp;
Way Home" post-credits scene. When Eddie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.040
is yanked out of the MCU, he leaves&nbsp;
behind a small piece of the Symbiote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.040
on the bar. It feels like a safe bet that&nbsp;
that bit of black goo will find its way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.960
one way or another, to Peter Parker.
Depending on what happens to that dollop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.960
of symbiote, Venom could theoretically have&nbsp;
a face-off with Spider-Man in the MCU now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.040
whether Tom Hardy is involved or not. And now&nbsp;
that the multiverse has been blown open for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.440
both characters, Eddie Brock could well make&nbsp;
a return visit in the future, or vice versa.&nbsp;

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.520
Venom tells Eddie in "Let There Be Carnage" that&nbsp;
the Symbiote Collective Mind knows all about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:05.840
the multiverse already. If a fight is in the&nbsp;
cards for them, Venom at least would be ready.&nbsp;

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.480
This all leaves us with just one question:&nbsp;
Who wins in a fight between Tom Holland's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.560
Spider-Man and Tom Hardy's Venom?&nbsp;
That's a topic for another day.
 &nbsp;

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:19.440
"On my planet, I am kind of a loser,&nbsp;
like you. But here, we could be more."
 &nbsp;

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.840
"Excuse me?"
 
